## PowerShell Reference Cheat Sheet

Active Directory is heavily managed via the `ActiveDirectory` PowerShell module. Below are the modern equivalents to standard identity workflows.

### Account Creation & Deletion
* **Create a user with a specific organizational path:**
  ```powershell
  New-ADUser -Name "Bob Smith" -SamAccountName "bob" -Path "OU=Employees,DC=domain,DC=local" -CreateHomeDirectory -HomeDrive "H:" -HomePath "\\server\homes\bob"
  ```
* **Delete a user and remove their directory objects:**
  ```powershell
  Remove-ADUser -Identity "bob" -Confirm:\$false
  ```

### Security & Password Management
* **Set or reset a user's password:**
  ```powershell
  Set-ADAccountPassword -Identity "joker" -NewPassword (Read-Host -AsSecureString "Enter Password")
  ```
* **Lock/Disable a user account:**
  ```powershell
  Disable-ADAccount -Identity "joker"
  ```
* **Unlock/Enable a user account:**
  ```powershell
  Enable-ADAccount -Identity "joker"
  ```
* **Check the status and properties of an account:**
  ```powershell
  Get-ADUser -Identity "joker" -Properties AccountLockoutTime, Enabled, PasswordLastSet
  ```

### Modifying Group Memberships
* **Add a user to a security group (e.g., Domain Admins):**
  ```powershell
  Add-ADGroupMember -Identity "Domain Admins" -Members "joker"
  ```
* **View all groups a specific user belongs to:**
  ```powershell
  Get-ADPrincipalGroupMembership -Identity "joker" | Select-Object Name
  ```

