## Active Directory Permissions (NTFS & Share)

Windows relies on Access Control Lists (ACLs) composed of Access Control Entries (ACEs) to protect resources.

### Standard Folder Permission Structure

| Security Principal | Inheritance | Permission Level | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Creator Owner** | None | Full Control | The user who creates subfiles owns them |
| **SYSTEM** | Inherited | Full Control | Operating system engine access |
| **Domain Admins** | Inherited | Full Control | Domain administrator structural access |
| **Target User** | Explicit | Modify / Read / Write | Granted personal access to their home share |
